    "body": "pulse task #2915 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:bc8507850a0f3d27b53223ffa155a3bb -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2915: Correct README and feature-matrix capability and format claims\n\nOperation: bc8507850a0f3d27b53223ffa155a3bb\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nPlanning split requested by user20 October2026; proposed Todo, no implementation start. Goal7, Hex0.1; baseline b05a9eaa. Preserve original parent acceptance/evidence and canonical PR. One focused child PR owns this step; parent PR retains overall integration/acceptance, not duplicate implementation. Production guards/source behavior unchanged. Required merge checks follow repository-resolved plan on exact candidate; focused tests are edit feedback, not a substitute.\nProblem/evidence F01: README:38\u201340 says warp/beat anchors exist while:236\u2013237 says future; format history emphasizes11 while public storage::encode at lib.rs:133\u2013136 emits33 at baseline; docs/features.md Projects row says29. README crate/dependency overview also predates current boundaries.\nChange: reconcile current-state capability/format/concise project-map statements in README.md and docs/features.md with actual encode/decode/render sources and specialized docs. Link the architecture map rather than duplicate detailed dependencies. Public writer33 is baseline evidence; recheck at execution. Never mistake intermediate DTO24 for public format.\nDone when: no contradictory warp/beat-anchor/editor claims; writer and supported-reader statements match actual dispatch; historical migration facts clearly labeled history and not current alpha obligations; native/listening gaps remain explicit; links resolve.\nScope prose only; no schema migration/reader cleanup, refactor or new verification claim.\nVerify: owning source comparison and prose merge plan. Low risk. Independent; coordinate architecture links with sibling crate-map step.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
